      "created_at": "2026-08-18T19:30:46Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-18T22:49:36Z",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "I'm able to reproduce the error by setting up a test node with a funded wallet and running getblocktemplate on the 1st thread with a longpoll ID on a second terminal to display result. And then, I ran `Cli stop` after sending funds on the first terminal triggers a 2nd thread to run the shut down process. \n\nThis happens on half of the attempts that I've tried. The other half exists normally with error -9 (Shut down)\n\n$ ./build/bin/bitcoin-cli -regtest -datadir=/tmp/gbtrepro getblocktemplate '{\"rules\":[\"segwit\"],\"longpollid\":\"4d9ad53b6b0cdda5d3e2f46ca3065053068dc7095d713034d355f237a783457c4\"}'\nerror code: -1\nerror message:\nInternal bug detected: block_template\n./rpc/mining.cpp:910 (getblocktemplate()::<lambda(const RPCMethod&, const JSONRPCRequest&)>)\nBitcoin Core v31.99.0-311847fffa21\nPlease report this issue here: https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues\n\n",
